# SHA-256 digests of the pinned Verus release assets.
#
# `prover-tools` matches the archive name in the second column against
# `verus-<version>-<target>.zip` and verifies the first column before unzipping
# (see `expected_sha256` in rust-prover-tools). Keep the two-space separator:
# that is the `sha256sum` output format the parser splits on.
#
# Digests are not published by the Verus release process, so each was computed
# locally from three independent downloads of the same asset, which agreed.
# Refresh a digest only by downloading the asset again and re-checking it.
#
# Regenerate for a new pin with:
#   curl -sSfL -o asset.zip \
#     https://github.com/verus-lang/verus/releases/download/release/<version>/verus-<version>-x86-linux.zip
#   sha256sum asset.zip
